[16.226597, "o", "Help on class Sandbox in module e2b.sandbox_sync.main:\r\n\r\nclass Sandbox(e2b.sandbox_sync.sandbox_api.SandboxApi)\r\n |  Sandbox(**opts: typing_extensions.Unpack[e2b.sandbox.main.SandboxOpts])\r\n |  \r\n |  E2B cloud sandbox is a secure and isolated cloud environment.\r\n |  \r\n |  The sandbox allows you to:\r\n |  - Access Linux OS\r\n |  - Create, list, and delete files and directories\r\n |  - Run commands\r\n |  - Run isolated code\r\n |  - Access the internet\r\n |  \r\n |  Check docs [here](https://e2b.dev/docs).\r\n |  \r\n |  Use the `Sandbox.create()` to create a new sandbox.\r\n |  \r\n |  Example:\r\n |  ```python\r\n |  from e2b import Sandbox\r\n |  \r\n |  sandbox = Sandbox.create()\r\n |  ```\r\n |  \r\n |  Method resolution order:\r\n |      Sandbox\r\n |      e2b.sandbox_sync.sandbox_api.SandboxApi\r\n |      e2b.sandbox.main.SandboxBase\r\n |      builtins.object\r\n |  \r\n |  Methods defined here:\r\n |  \r\n |  __enter__(self)\r\n |  \r\n |  __exit__(self, exc_type, exc_value, traceback)\r\n |  \r\n |  __init__(self, **opts: typing_extensions.Unpack[e2b.sa"]
[16.22949, "o", "ndbox.main.SandboxOpts])\r\n |      :deprecated: This constructor is deprecated\r\n |      \r\n |      Use `Sandbox.create()` to create a new sandbox instead.\r\n |  \r\n |  beta_pause(self, **opts: typing_extensions.Unpack[e2b.connection_config.ApiParams]) -> None\r\n |      [BETA] This feature is in beta and may change in the future.\r\n |      \r\n |      Pause the sandbox.\r\n |      \r\n |      :return: Sandbox ID that can be used to resume the sandbox\r\n |  \r\n |  connect(self, timeout: Optional[int] = None, **opts: typing_extensions.Unpack[e2b.connection_config.ApiParams]) -> typing_extensions.Self\r\n |      Connect to a sandbox. If the sandbox is paused, it will be REDACTEDmatically resumed.\r\n |      Sandbox must be either running or be paused.\r\n |      \r\n |      With sandbox ID you can connect to the same sandbox from different places or environments (serverless functions, etc).\r\n |      \r\n |      :param timeout: Timeout for the sandbox in **seconds**.\r\n |          For running sandboxes, the timeout will update only if the new"]
[16.229501, "o", " timeout is longer than the existing one.\r\n |      :retur"]
[16.229673, "o", "n: A running sandbox instance\r\n |      \r\n |      @example\r\n |      ```python\r\n |      sandbox = Sandbox.create()\r\n |      sandbox.beta_pause()\r\n |      \r\n |      # Another code block\r\n |      same_sandbox = sandbox.connect()\r\n |      ```\r\n |  \r\n |  create_snapshot(self, **opts: typing_extensions.Unpack[e2b.connection_config.ApiParams]) -> e2b.sandbox.sandbox_api.SnapshotInfo\r\n |      Create a snapshot of the sandbox's current state.\r\n |      \r\n |      The sandbox will be paused while the snapshot is being created.\r\n |      The snapshot can be used to create new sandboxes with the same filesystem and state.\r\n |      Snapshots are persistent and survive sandbox deletion.\r\n |      \r\n |      Use the returned `snapshot_id` with `Sandbox.create(snapshot_id)` to create a new sandbox from the snapshot.\r\n |      \r\n |      :return: Snapshot information including the snapshot ID\r\n |  \r\n |  get_info(self, **opts: typing_extensions.Unpack[e2b.connection_config.ApiParams]) -> e2b.sandbox.sandbox_api.SandboxInfo\r\n"]
